From 8c4297fd68bd92fe4c600a2ef6182c08bf3869d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:10:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Appearance: color wheel picker, themed Settings, fixes for
 extra keys and wallpaper

- Extra keys: buttons start in the same background they return to when released,
  and that background is transparent while a wallpaper is on, so keys that have
  been pressed no longer look held down over the wallpaper
- Wallpaper keeps one size when the keyboard opens (StableWallpaperView remembers
  the keyboard-down height; the parent clips the rest)
- Settings top bar, status bar, switches and sliders follow the terminal theme by
  default, or Termux red, or a custom color (Appearance > Settings look)
- Color editor: color wheel + brightness slider + hex field in one dialog, and a
  name and description under every color
- ColorMath: Android-free HSV/hex/contrast helpers

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016cyqPmKVt5ExSeVFn51HQf
